1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,461
Open Archived Calls from the Omni Dispatch menu to review calls that have already closed.

2
00:00:05,641 --> 00:00:11,743
This is useful when a caller asks about earlier activity or a team needs context for a follow-up.

3
00:00:12,063 --> 00:00:16,031
Choose Filters to see the available choices, including Closed As.

4
00:00:16,211 --> 00:00:20,819
Use the status filter to focus on the type of closeout you need to review.

5
00:00:21,139 --> 00:00:24,275
Use the search box to find the archived call by name.

6
00:00:24,455 --> 00:00:27,100
Here we find the fictional community standby.

7
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:30,523
Check the call number and closed status before opening it.

8
00:00:30,843 --> 00:00:34,725
Call Details keeps the original description with its call number.

9
00:00:34,905 --> 00:00:39,343
A security dispatcher could use it to identify an earlier site incident.

10
00:00:39,523 --> 00:00:43,917
A wildland contractor could use it to confirm which exercise was closed.

11
00:00:44,237 --> 00:00:49,208
Open History to review previous calls at this location when they are available.

12
00:00:49,388 --> 00:00:54,636
Check the exact call number and the details before using an earlier call as context.
